<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Soccer-Results of FAI Cup first round ties.</title>
<headline>Soccer-Results of FAI Cup first round ties.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Football Association of Ireland (FAI) challenge cup first round ties played on Sunday.</p>
<p>    Shamrock Rovers    5    Limerick		 4</p>
<p>After extra-time. The sides were level 3-3 after 90 minutes.</p>
<p>    Garda F.C.	   0     Drogheda United     2</p>
<p>After extra-time</p>
<p>    Cork City	    2     Galway United	 0</p>
<p>    Wayside Celtic     2     Finn Harps	    1</p>
<p>    Kilkenny City	1     Bohemians	     2</p>
<p>    Whitehall Rangers  0     Dundalk		 0</p>
<p>After extra-time. Replay at Oriel Park, Dundalk, on Wednesday, January 15, at 1945 GMT.</p>
<p>    Valeview Shankill  0    Rockmount		1</p>
<p>Played Saturday</p>
<p>    Longford Town		 0  St.Francis	1</p>
<p>    Derry City		    5  Crumlin United  0</p>
<p>    University College Dublin 0  Bray Wanderers  1</p>
<p>    Home Farm/Everton	   2  Glenmore Celtic 1</p>
<p>    Cobh Ramblers		 0  Sligo Rovers    3</p>
<p>    Dublin University	   4  Parkvilla F.C.  0</p>
<p>Played Friday</p>
<p>    Shelbourne		    4  Everton (Cork)  2</p>
<p>    St.Patrick's Athletic     1   Athlone Town   0</p>
<p>--Damien Lynch, Dublin newsroom 353-1-61-3377.</p>
